<title>UK: IEA supply/demand highlights - end-August report.</title>
<headline>IEA supply/demand highlights - end-August report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table highlights the oil supply-demand and stock estimates included in the International Energy Agency's latest Monthly Oil Market Report. Figures in million barrels per day.</p>
<p>		  1994 1Q95 2Q95 3Q95 4Q95 1995 1Q96 2Q96 3Q96 4Q96 1996 1Q97 1997</p>
<p>DEMAND</p>
<p> OECD	   40.0 41.0 39.1 39.7 41.3 40.3 42.1 39.7 40.7 41.9 41.1 42.5 41.7</p>
<p> NON-OECD     28.8 30.2 29.2 29.0 30.7 29.8 30.9 30.1 30.0 31.8 30.7 32.2 32.0</p>
<p> TOTAL	  68.8 71.2 68.3 68.7 72.0 70.1 73.0 69.8 70.6 73.6 71.8 74.8 73.6</p>
<p>SUPPLY</p>
<p> NON-OPEC     41.5 42.5 42.1 42.4 42.9 42.5 43.3 43.2 43.7 45.2 43.9 45.4 45.6</p>
<p> OPEC CRUDE   27.0 27.2 27.3 27.6 27.8 27.5 28.2 28.2</p>
<p> OPEC NGLS     2.4  2.4  2.4  2.4  2.5  2.4  2.5  2.6  2.7  2.8  2.6  2.7  2.8</p>
<p> TOTAL OPEC   27.0 27.2 27.3 27.6 27.8 27.5 28.2 28.2</p>
<p>TOTAL SUPPLY 68.6 69.7 69.4 70.1 70.7 69.9 71.5 71.4</p>
<p> OPEC CALL*   24.9 26.3 23.9 23.9 26.7 25.2 27.2 24.0 24.2 25.6 25.3 26.7 25.2</p>
<p>IND STOCKS    +0.1 -1.3 +0.7 +0.4 -1.3 -0.4 -1.2 +1.0</p>
<p>TOT STCK BAL -0.2 -1.5 +1.1 +1.4 -1.3 -0.2 -1.5  1.6</p>
<p> FSU NET EXP   2.4  2.0  2.7  2.6  2.2  2.4  2.4  2.8  2.8  2.3  2.6  2.6  2.8</p>
<p>* Implied call on OPEC crude equals total demand minus total non-OPEC supply minus OPEC NGLs. Thus includes &quot;miscellaneous to balance&quot; for historical time periods.</p>
<p>Figures have been adjusted to take account of Gabon's departure from OPEC, ratified at the group's 100th ministerial meeting in Vienna in June but effective from January 1995.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
